From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:02:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dashboard): session-scoped model.options handoff without
 stalling the loop [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem: Independent review of PR #3757 at 0ae22c212b requested changes.
Owner-routed Desktop model.options sends session_id without profile, so the
busy predecessor forwarded a launch-profile catalog and the successor's
disk-config model. Async GET /api/model/options ran the 5s urllib GET on
the event loop (1.02s stall with a 1s stub). Query builders, loopback GET,
and pop_backend_port -> this_backend_port were untested.

Why 1: Handoff copied params.profile only; Desktop omits it for tiles.
Why 2: Successor load_picker_context is that profile's launch/disk config,
not the live agent pick still owned by the predecessor session.
Why 3: get_model_options already offloads the picker build via
run_in_threadpool; the new handoff path did not.
Root: Control-read forwarding was unscoped and synchronous on the busy
predecessor.

Countermeasures:
- symptom: derive successor profile from session profile_home (refuse
  unknown session scope); overlay live agent model/provider on the result;
  await handoff_control_read in run_in_threadpool.
- root: shared model_options_control_path (lowercase bools); successor
  port must be in BACKEND_PORTS; writes/prompts still unforwarded.
- detection: cross-profile/live-model, unknown-session, event-loop ticker,
  real _loopback_control_get (token/HTTPError/None/non-dict), query
  builders, pop_backend_port binding.

Proof: scripts/run_tests.sh test_always_on_control_handoff.py +
test_always_on_rollover.py + test_dashboard_session_token_routes.py +
test_code_skew.py + test_model_rpc_skew_guard.py +
test_model_options_profile_scope.py — 76 passed.

Limits: still read-only GET /api/model/options + model.options RPC.
Not queue migration or live model switching.
